 "requested_at": "2026-11-13T20:15:01.862070Z",
 "text": "Under the *Residential Tenancies Act, 2006* (RTA), a landlord has a non-waivable statutory duty to maintain the rental unit in a good state of repair and fit for habitation, as well as in compliance with all applicable health, safety, housing, and maintenance standards. \n\nSubsection 20(2) specifically provides that this duty applies even if the tenant was aware of the state of disrepair before entering into the tenancy agreement. Furthermore, under section 4 of the RTA, any lease provision that is inconsistent with the Act is void. Therefore, a clause waiving the landlord’s obligation to fix a broken window is of no force or effect.\n\nVerdict: not enforceable\nSection: 20",
